    <string name="app_tour_gauge_title">Lean-angle gauge</string>
    <string name="app_tour_gauge_body">The needle shows the current lean angle. MAX L and MAX R are your persistent gauge records: they survive app restarts and rides and only increase through measured lean. Long-press the gauge, or use the Settings button, to reset both without changing any recorded ride.</string>
    <string name="app_tour_recording_title">Record a ride</string>
    <string name="app_tour_recording_body">On the first recording start, the app explains and requests location and notification permissions. GPS records the route, speed, and distance; Stop finishes and saves the ride.</string>
    <string name="app_tour_pause_title">Pause and automation</string>
    <string name="app_tour_pause_body">Pause recording when you want to exclude a section. Auto-Pause protects the recording during extreme rotation; when purchased and enabled, Auto Resume can continue after movement is detected again.</string>
    <string name="app_tour_live_data_title">Live ride data</string>
    <string name="app_tour_live_data_body">The history graph shows recent lean values. During GPS recording, the dashboard also shows speed, distance, and elapsed riding time.</string>
    <string name="app_tour_history_title">History and details</string>
    <string name="app_tour_history_body">Finished rides appear in History with their recorded maximum lean and point count. Open a ride to inspect its route, graphs, and statistics and jump to important points.</string>
    <string name="app_tour_manage_title">Manage and configure</string>
    <string name="app_tour_manage_body">In History you can select, combine, rename, or delete rides. Settings controls recording interval, live-history length, calibration, and lets you restart this tour at any time.</string>
